# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Curio auth-web project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 as a dependency
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Code Integration
- Modified `src/App.tsx` to integrate analytics:
  - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the main app div, after the bottom navigation
  
### Implementation Details
- Following the official Vercel documentation for React applications
- The Analytics component was placed at the root level of the application (in App.tsx)
- Positioned after all route content and the bottom navigation for optimal tracking
- The component is inside the ThemeProvider and main app container to ensure it has access to the full React context

### Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ Linter passed with no new errors (`npm run lint`)
- ✅ Lock file updated with new dependencies
- ✅ Package.json properly includes @vercel/analytics in dependencies

## Next Steps
Once this is deployed to Vercel:
1. Navigate to the Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
2. Click the "Enable" button to activate analytics
3. Verify analytics are working by checking browser Network tab for requests to the analytics endpoint

## Framework Details
- Project: React 19.2.8 with Vite 8.2.0
- Analytics Package: @vercel/analytics/react (framework-specific for React)
- Integration follows React best practices with component-based architecture
